[block'glyph-rust-whole'
  [ctx'Glyph 100% in Rust, the engine, the core of the app and the skill, with the JS leaving piece by piece; this is the spec of EMS-002, the second series of orders Glyph emits, and it commissions the series and implements nothing','the repository root','engine 3.6.9.07, EMS-001 closed from ORD-0001 to ORD-0012 and waiting at the gate of ORD-0013']
  [skl'glyph-markup'[ins'hear this spec, ground before building, and stop at the gate of the Regent']]

  [section'species'
    [dfn'virtual path','file, delimiter and selector: the extension decides how the selector reads, and the path resolves to one exact slice with offsets']
    [dfn'index','.guidelines/.shortcuts/.virtual/index.json, the durable state the engine writes and a resolver without judgement reads']
    [dfn'sources','the list a document declares in its frontmatter: the slices it is written from, each a virtual path']
    [nt'the ORD count resets in each series: EMS-002 counts from ORD-0001']
    [nt'the vocabulary of the project lives in .guidelines/GLOSSARY.md section 8']
  ]

  [section'direction'
    [intn'Glyph 100% in Rust: the JS leaves piece by piece, each piece when the Rust passes the oracle on it']
    [cnst'until a piece leaves, the JS is the reference, and it changes only where the oracle must change']
    [cnst'a capability with no JS counterpart is built in Rust only']
    [cnst'every crate passes the graded filter of .constraints: note enters vendored, ask enters with an ADR the Regent signs, fix is refused']
    [nt'EMS-001 closes as written, at ORD-0014, and this series does not reopen it']
  ]

  [section'queue'
    [cnst'an ORD enters the queue when the Regent calls it, and its number is its place in the queue']
    [nt'the candidates are the items decided and not built in .guidelines/.plan/README.md section 5']
    [nt'the EMS.json of this series enters with the ORD that builds the EMS configuration; until then its rules live in this spec']
  ]

  [section'exceptions'
    [exc]
  ]

  [section'ORD-0001-virtual-paths'
    [tgt'glyph-vpath: the virtual paths of .plan section 0, layers 1, 4, 5 and 6, keyed by the slug']
    [nt'measured before the code, INTAKE-VIRTUAL-PATH sections 18 and 19: a stale source is fix, the fingerprint is per node, sources starts from the seeds of M3, and the slug keys this ORD']
    [nt'the NodeID, order maintenance and the recovery index, layers 2, 3 and 7, are ORDs of their own']
    [val'the trees','the extension decides the selector: .md by heading slug, .json by JSON Pointer, .xml by element path, code and text by @block and @endblock; an empty selector is the whole file; zero nodes or many is an error, never an empty slice']
    [val'the index','every file of .guidelines, the attic and the index aside, with README.md and CLAUDE.md, in the index; each node with its byte range, its line range and its fingerprint, and every entry resolves to content that is not empty']
    [val'the resolver','many paths read each file once, the answer carries the offsets, the slice arrives under its own virtual path, and a fingerprint that no longer matches is refused']
    [val'sources','a document declares its sources in its frontmatter, the index answers which documents a file feeds by inversion, and the seeds of INTAKE-VIRTUAL-PATH section 19 enter']
    [val'the gate','npm run check refuses an index that drifted, a file left out, a source that does not resolve and a stale source, each seen failing before it counts']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0002-node-id'
    [onlyif'ORD-0001 closed']
    [tgt'glyph-vpath: the NodeID, layer 2 of .plan section 0, identity carried by structure alone']
    [nt'measured before the code, INTAKE-VIRTUAL-PATH sections 20 and 21: structure recovers 113 of 124 breaks whose content lived on; a heading renamed over a changed body is layer 7']
    [val'the identity','every node carries a NodeID that passes from one build to the next by the same path, the same text, the same body or the same file renamed, and a NodeID resolves to its node in constant time']
    [val'the aliases','the old path of a node that moved resolves to the node it became, with a warning naming the new path, and never blocks']
    [val'the gate','npm run check refuses a source declared by an old path and an index whose identities, parents or aliases do not hold, each seen failing before it counts']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0003-recovery'
    [onlyif'ORD-0002 closed']
    [tgt'glyph-vpath: the recovery index, layer 7 of .plan section 0, by the content']
    [nt'measured before the code, INTAKE-VIRTUAL-PATH sections 22 and 23: by the path, precision 35.7 percent and recall 41.7 percent; layer 7 recovers by the content']
    [val'the recovery','a heading renamed while its body changes is found again by its old path and its old NodeID, and a deletion is not']
    [val'the index miss','every answer through a recovery warns with its score, never blocks, and is written to the log of misses']
    [val'the gate','npm run check refuses a source declared by a recovered path and an index whose recoveries do not hold, each seen failing before it counts']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0004-order'
    [onlyif'ORD-0003 closed']
    [tgt'glyph-vpath: order maintenance, layer 3 of .plan section 0, as order queries over the positions the index holds']
    [nt'measured before the code, INTAKE-VIRTUAL-PATH sections 24 and 25: an edit shifts 42.0 percent of the rows it rewrites, under the 50 percent declared; the positions stay absolute']
    [val'before','for any two references, before answers which comes first, or that one holds the other, in constant time']
    [val'above and between','above answers what precedes a node in its file, nearest first, and between the nodes from one reference to another in order, each by a search in logarithmic time']
    [val'the order','the order agrees with the files and offsets of the index on every pair, and answers right after a node is inserted, moved or removed']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0005-astral'
    [tgt'a declared source with characters outside the BMP, question 2 of the EMS-001 return, answered a']
    [val'the source','a declared source whose literals and prose carry characters outside the BMP enters the corpus, and the snapshot moves by decision, no earlier hash moved']
    [val'the oracle','the Rust answers the new case byte for byte, and every module the export writes']
    [val'the survivor','lev counting characters instead of UTF-16 units, the mutant no case of the oracle killed, dies']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0006-rules-cache'
    [tgt'the compiled rules leave the rules store, question 3 of the EMS-001 return, answered a']
    [val'the JS first','the JS keeps its compiled rules off the store object, and the envelope hashes the rules store alone']
    [val'the snapshot','the ast hashes move by decision, and no xml or hgml hash moves']
    [val'the Rust follows','glyph_rules::with_cache leaves, the Rust answers the moved oracle byte for byte, and the pin that held the cache in the digest is inverted']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0007-json'
    [tgt'JSON in a crate of its own under every other, question 4 of the EMS-001 return, answered b']
    [val'the crate','glyph-json holds what glyph_util::json held and replaces the Value of glyph-stores, one JSON type for the workspace']
    [val'the graph','crate-graph.js names glyph-json with its oracle, as the floor every crate may reach and that reaches none, seen failing before it counts']
    [val'the oracle','every crate answers the oracle as before, byte for byte']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0008-registered'
    [tgt'a template body reads what the caller registered, question 6 of the EMS-001 return, answered c']
    [val'the registry','the Rust keeps what the caller registered beside the context, and a template body reads it, as the JS body reads useRules and useExpansions']
    [val'the callers','the CLI and the engine behind the app register the repository stores in both engines, the JS protocol first, so a body that breaks a rule reads the same in the CLI and in the app by both engines']
    [val'the oracle','the export records template bodies with nothing registered and with the repository registered, the Rust answers both byte for byte, and the oracle of the cases does not move']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0009-zip'
    [tgt'the zip of a series ORD only behind a flag, question 1 of the EMS-001 return, answered c']
    [val'the flag','in a series, --bundle writes the folder and, with --zip, the zip beside it, in both engines, the JS first']
    [val'the oracle','the export runs the flag in a series and outside one, and the Rust answers the same bytes and the same files']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0010-classify'
    [tgt'classify answered by the page from the tables it loads, question 10 of the EMS-001 return, answered c']
    [val'the requests','behind engine=relay, every call but classify is one request, and classify is answered by the page; L-01 stops making 8 000 trips']
    [val'the panels','the declared sources give the same bytes in every panel through the relay and through the JS']
    [val'the swap','the suite holds the calls the transport swaps to the eleven, seen failing before it counts']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0011-case-stores'
    [tgt'the snapshot honours the stores of each case, O5 of INTAKE-RUST-LADDER, answered on 2026-09-27']
    [val'the snapshot','each declared case is projected with its own stores laid over the repository ones, the T hashes move by decision, and no other hash moves']
    [val'the oracle','TemplateCycle enters the oracle, the case files and the runs say which stores a case brings, and the Rust answers them byte for byte']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0012-crate-weight'
    [tgt'the ruler of the crates at the gate, O7 of INTAKE-RUST-LADDER, answered on 2026-09-27']
    [val'the ruler','check:rust measures the tree of every external crate as INTAKE-RUST-LADDER section 9 measures it, and grades it note, ask or fix as .constraints says']
    [val'the grades','note enters, ask enters only with an ADR the Regent signed, fix is refused; each seen failing before it counts']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0013-once'
    [tgt'the Rust stops redoing on every call what the JS does once, question 12 of the EMS-001 return, answered b on 2026-09-27']
    [val'the digest','ck in integer arithmetic answers the bytes the JS writes']
    [val'the stores','a store is shared and never copied, and the rules compile once a store']
    [val'the bytes','no emitted byte moves, and the JS is not tuned']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0014-renames'
    [tgt'the renames that move the emitted output, O8, O9 and O10 of INTAKE-RUST-LADDER, answered on 2026-09-27, the first ORD of the batch the version moves once for']
    [val'sceptic','SKEP emits sceptic, and the former spelling skeptic is still read, in the source and in the XML, and named']
    [val'mould and template','the diagnostic says template, preset leaves the stores, the comment of an empty source says mould, and the key of the saved moulds migrates once without losing one']
    [val'frame','the vocabulary category of the structure and template pieces is frame']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0015-ref'
    [tgt'the reference syntax, a name a reference writes and nothing binds asks for it outside the logic fence, answered on 2026-09-27, the second ORD of the batch']
    [val'the reference','a name-shaped literal under REF that no command of the document binds raises an ask and emits needs var beside the literal; a bound name keeps its ref, and prose stays prose']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0016-deep'
    [tgt'the deep-inference alarm, a composite of depth 5 or more with no operand asks, answered on 2026-09-27, the third ORD of the batch']
    [val'the alarm','a composite of depth 5 or more, with no operand and no frame or slot that asks for one, raises an ask and emits needs; a chain link is not asked, as with every frame']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0017-part-if'
    [tgt'the two proposals of the XML draft, the number of a part and the condition of an if as attributes, answered on 2026-09-27, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the attributes','the operand literal of PT becomes n of part and that of IF becomes cond of if, when it carries nothing else; fromXML reads both back as the literal']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0018-blend'
    [tgt'the blend REV and DIST only on the same target, answered on 2026-09-27, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the target','the atoms of a blend fuse when they work on one subject, and different subjects burn as separate commands']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0019-o4-semicolons'
    [tgt'the first residual of O4, in the Rust only: the line break between two blocks burns as its own line, answered on 2026-10-25, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the mark','the Rust writes the line ;; between two blocks where a segment break writes the blank line']
    [val'the known difference','the oracle tests name the difference, undo it before comparing, and hold everything else byte for byte']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0020-o4-quotes'
    [tgt'the second residual of O4, in the Rust only: inside a literal only the quote that opened it closes it, a line break as well, answered on 2026-10-25, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the quote','an apostrophe literal runs past a line break to its own quote or to the bracket, as the backtick does and as the grammar says']
    [val'the known difference','the oracle test names each source it reaches with the tokens the decision gives it']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0021-o4-bare'
    [tgt'the third residual of O4, in the Rust only: a bare word where a template parameter goes is refused by name, answered on 2026-10-25, the last free ORD of the batch']
    [val'the refusal','a bare word in a parameter position raises TemplateParamNotLiteral naming the word, with the arguments as the author wrote them, quoted']
    [val'the known difference','the oracle names each source it reaches with the diagnostics the decision gives it']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0022-mood-return'
    [tgt'a mood in a return segment reaches the XML, the first of the inclusions decided on 2026-10-25, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the mood','a mood written in a return segment emits mood first in its block, ahead of user-expectative, and both ways back keep the return marker']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0023-mood-template'
    [tgt'a mood inside a template, the Rust answers and the JS throws until it leaves, answered on 2026-10-25, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the known difference','the four sources the oracle records the JS throwing are named with the document the Rust answers']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0024-modes'
    [tgt'the mode words never vanish, a stray on, an off at the end, and the bare words, answered on 2026-10-25, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the modes','a stray on is the command on with a note, an off at the end raises UnclosedOffMode, and the bare words join the loose-word check']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0025-chains'
    [tgt'a known command after an operand, a space or a closing bracket is a chain link, answered on 2026-10-25, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the links','a dash touching a known name after an operand, a space or a closing bracket makes a chain link, and prose stays prose']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0026-placeholder'
    [tgt'a command held by a placeholder reaches the XML, answered on 2026-10-25 with the placeholder wrapper, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the placeholder','a placeholder holding more than its name and question emits placeholder with the needs where the question was written, then the rest, and a second bare tag is a chain link']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0027-ast-space'
    [tgt'the way back writes the space a name needs from the prose after it, an inclusion of 2026-10-25, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the space','fromAST writes a space between a command name or a mood header and the prose after it, so a known command never turns unknown on the way back']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0028-template-fills'
    [tgt'what a template call carries never vanishes, the commands inside a fill, a fill naming no parameter, and a template defined in the source, answered on 2026-10-25, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the fills','a command inside a named fill travels with its value carrying the slot, an unknown fill lands after the body with TemplateUnknownParam, and a source definition expands its calls']
  ]

  [section'ORD-0029-links'
    [tgt'the further positions where a known name touching a dash starts a chain link, answered on 2026-10-26 with the same rule, an ORD of the batch']
    [val'the links','a known name touching a dash that starts a word is a chain link of the scope it is in, and prose stays prose']
  ]

  [section'limits'
    [nev'a selector that answers an empty slice in silence']
    [dont'open an ORD before the ORD it depends on closes']
    [cnst'prose declares the state, never the correction']
    [cnst'no worktrees']
  ]

  [section'conclude'
    [ins'update the where-am-I table of .shortcuts at each ORD that closes']
    [--track
      [ph-item'each ORD of the series, the commit that closed it and the digest it matched']
      [ph-scope'EMS-002']
    ]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0001, glyph-vpath: the trees by extension, the index of 134 files in 1 750 nodes with bytes, lines and fingerprint, the resolver, sources seeded and the gate in npm run check, each breach seen failing, at b8bcbe3 and 6f8a1c2; sha256 fc5b4f241ff9b345cdb7d9ef994e9c51211683a0a4543b186dca31160b2f9c69 of the index at 6f8a1c2'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0002, the NodeID: identity carried by structure alone, five rules in order, the parent of each node in the index, old paths as aliases that answer with a warning, node and up, and the gate that refuses a source by an old path and an identity that does not hold; the migration gave n1 to n1789 to the index of ORD-0001; at 1abdc2a, sha256 4b327f203896c592cb9508b317a5cf56aea5120ff2792e4840d30e3fe6433213 of the index at 1abdc2a'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0003, the recovery index by the content: a section the NodeID does not reach comes back as the successor with the largest line-set Jaccard, at least 0.5 and unique, without identity; the old text from the cache or from git, checked by its fingerprint; an answer through a recovery warns with its score and goes to the log of misses; the gate refuses a source by a recovered path and a recovery that does not hold; at 2440e38, sha256 7ea852e9661be01d5f736f202de4290460d4462796b63cd1c52a8b5089334215 of the index at 2440e38'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0004, order maintenance as order queries over the positions of the index: the order sorted once on load, before in constant time, above and between by search; nothing new stored, and stable positions by Dietz–Sleator refused by M7; at 94a4d09, sha256 dfecdf9d4fc96da84fe6c67c8fccdbaabb95ec0dec4cd89213492e4a0e766b03 of the index at 94a4d09, against which the order was proved on every one of 1.7 million pairs'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0005, the declared source outside the BMP: P-35, the snapshot from 114 to 115 sources by decision, no earlier hash moved; the Rust answers the new case byte for byte, and lev counting characters, the mutant the oracle of 114 cases left alive, dies; at 2f8dd85, sha256 5fd8784b5189bee185663f843c225b37d2948502fb0d4dcaaf67a60ab443c9e0 of the 115 case files and b97a1d0ef781f8779704f6262613208084182b70eb34bfb09dfec6b756f3b3d5 of util.json'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0006, the compiled rules off the store: the JS keeps them in a WeakMap keyed by the store, the envelope hashes the store alone, the 115 ast hashes moved by decision and no xml or hgml hash; with_cache leaves the Rust, and the pin that held the cache in the digest inverted; at 37be708, sha256 86600fec025a1db860876091c6ba2df68c80ecdad1129f588cd06af9e5cfec83 of the cases, a1b8cee2754a0b5bd5a3799f9ed2447dbb38c085c95097b9f9abcd9239a940c1 of ast.json and 2c41220c1dd911afa6271839da73154c5bc6417bf627ffd48b0bd664d30ef119 of stores.json'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0007, JSON in a crate of its own: glyph-json holds what glyph_util::json held and replaces the Value of glyph-stores, one JSON type for the workspace; crate-graph.js names it as the floor, with the platform as its oracle, seen failing before it counts; no projection moved; at ab37357, sha256 86600fec025a1db860876091c6ba2df68c80ecdad1129f588cd06af9e5cfec83 of the cases, the digest of ORD-0006'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0008, a template body reads what the caller registered: the Registered of the Rust beside the context, the repository one in the CLI and in glyph-engine; the JS protocol registers when it runs as the engine; registry.json holds 63 probes in both states, and a body that breaks a rule reads the same in the CLI and in the app by both engines; the oracle of the cases did not move; at 64f995a, sha256 4a245e6c231a0f9003fafe0dfe510cdd96297a6ec5085b3c20a0f5ec34914494 of registry.json and 86600fec025a1db860876091c6ba2df68c80ecdad1129f588cd06af9e5cfec83 of the cases'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0009, the zip of a series ORD only behind a flag: --zip in both engines, the JS first, the ORD-####.zip beside the folder without moving the count; the README and the bundle command of the plugin document it, and the export runs it in a series and outside one; at f038b9c, sha256 487a2691f110814bc6ea9024ab16ade6157633d22f818a0a5383514d14ee3cd8 of cli.json, 731 runs, written on Linux'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0010, classify answered by the page from the tables it loads: behind engine=relay one request a call but classify; RL-16 holds the swap set; measured in Chromium through serve-dev.js, the 115 sources typed, from 11 163 requests to 575, L-01 from 8 005 a keystroke to 5, no panel different, by the JS engine and by the Rust; at 936e91d, sha256 5c3228dcd2f1609ff08325bf6c27bd8fcb1979902001d18e6d5304f9ab8a4c95 of glyph-transport.js'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0011, the snapshot honours the stores of each case: the case stores laid over the repository ones in the snapshot, the case files and the runs; T-07, T-08 and T-09 moved by decision and no other; TemplateCycle in the oracle; Context::with in the Rust; at e900c7a, sha256 7dcf5a1121360749d482c02bc9a8d23806f47626315c4cf0cce876432140a318 of the cases'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0012, the ruler of the crates at the gate: scripts/crate-weight.js in check:rust measures the tree of every external crate as section 9 measures it and grades note, ask and fix; ask enters only with an ADR signed in .decisions; seen failing on recorded trees, one for each grade; the workspace holds no external crate today; at 18b4392, sha256 82812a7cf6624f95ec7327870cd1e0a4c443f4773779076ebd78100845c3c79e of crate-weight.js'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0013, the Rust stops redoing on every call what the JS does once: ck in integer arithmetic around its product, which stays a double; the stores behind an Arc, shared by a template body and by the formula of a composite; the rules compiled once a store in compiled_of, keyed by the store, the port of compiledOf; the Parse without a copy of the rules store; four mutants seen failing; on the bench, release, the empty parse from 19.5 to 0.53 µs and the empty toAST from 8 034 to 285; no emitted byte moved; at bf89f46, sha256 7dcf5a1121360749d482c02bc9a8d23806f47626315c4cf0cce876432140a318 of the cases, the digest of ORD-0011'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0014, the renames that move the emitted output, the first of the batch of the version: SKEP emits sceptic, and the former spelling skeptic is read in the source and in the XML with a note, through FORMER_ELEMENT; template and mould where molde said template, in the diagnostic, the two stores and the comment of an empty source; the key of the saved moulds migrates once without losing one; the category frame; the snapshot moved by decision, the xml of L-04 and the 115 ast; six mutants seen failing, and two instruments in Chromium, the migration and the category; at 4d07028, sha256 e76297b484c723e60e54641bf524ce11ef98a38ca0b7396ae13f03cf35ae13ed of the cases'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0015, the reference syntax, the second of the batch of the version: a name-shaped literal under REF that no command of the package binds raises an ask, UnboundReference, and writes needs var beside the literal, which stays; a binding written later resolves; prose under REF asks nothing; the way back drops the needs; no hash of the snapshot moved; four probes in the oracle and BD-07 to BD-10; three mutants seen failing; at d0c8328, sha256 e76297b484c723e60e54641bf524ce11ef98a38ca0b7396ae13f03cf35ae13ed of the cases, the digest of ORD-0014, and 13e2509753ffd34980932536c417ef0e6fe4d7ebb5cd24b14bde31cd48049f63 of parse.json'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
    [--track[ph-item'ORD-0016, the deep-inference alarm, the third of the batch of the version: a composite of depth 5 or more with no operand, where no frame and no ordered slot asks, raises an ask, DeepInference, and writes needs the subject, by GLOSSARY section 0.3; where a frame asks, the question is its own; a chain link is not asked; today only FBK falls in it; no hash of the snapshot moved; six probes in the oracle and DI-01 to DI-05; three mutants seen failing; at 29400d2, sha256 e76297b484c723e60e54641bf524ce11ef98a38ca0b7396ae13f03cf35ae13ed of the cases, the digest of ORD-0014, and 8ad19cc250ec245118fa26f89b7e7001943da04df2ac489e8395657a81228725 of parse.json'][ph-scope'EMS-002']]
